  itemDescription: Space Technologies Institute  This institute leads R&D in space
    science and satellite technology. Its mission encompasses designing, building,
    and testing satellites (for Earth observation, communications, etc.), developing
    space instrumentation, and supporting national space missions. Focus areas include
    small satellite development (KACST has built Earth observation satellites like
    Saudisat), satellite payloads (cameras, sensors), and ground station technologies.
    The institute also trains engineers in spacecraft engineering and works closely
    with the Saudi Space Commission. By advancing indigenous space tech, it aims
    to ensure Saudi Arabia has independent capabilities in satellite deployment for
    applications like remote sensing, weather monitoring, and secure communications
  description: 
